From 6e903137fc390ec629436475233c495606ab86a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:22:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): restore a Board-restored card's hub
 delivery subscriptions from its chat links

kanban_notify_subs is machine-local, so a worker reprovisioned from the Board
(worker-1, 2026-11-11 ~21:43Z) got its cards and task_chat_links back but no
platform='hub' subscriptions. The hermes-hub collector derives a card's
published `sessions` (and the notifier its deliveries) only from those rows:
100 of 215 restored cards were republished with sessions=[] and their origin
chats on other gateways stopped hearing from them (t_01a1cf4cfd7eb125).

The sync apply now records an own-partition card it inserts into a primary
live board file (our own cards are only ever inserted by the feed on a
restore) in the local-only kanban_restored_cards, and each new
task_chat_links row of such a card that existed at the restore, is
unreleased and names a chat on another gateway with an exact profile gets
its `<gw>/<profile>/<session>` hub subscription back: caught up (no replay),
reason origin for a created link and shepherd for a shepherd link, owning
wins for one chat. NULL profile is never widened to 'default'; released,
local-gateway, placeholder/headless, archived, replica (sync-shadow),
link-only (sync-links) and foreign picked-up copies are skipped, and a link
that arrives later for a card this file already held never resurrects a
subscription retired on purpose.

Chosen over (b) deriving sessions from links in the hermes-hub collector,
which would fix publication but leave notice delivery dead and ship through a
separate repo, and (c) syncing kanban_notify_subs, whose cursors/in-flight
columns are per-machine delivery state.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_restore_origin_subs.py (RED 4/5 on
the base: restored subs [] and the installed collector published
sessions=[]; GREEN 5/5), plus 76 kanban sync/chat-link/worker-node/notify/
origin test files, 1242 passed.
